{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Mine</b> — the sense of Shechem and Succoth, which belong to Joseph; therefore Gilead and Manasseh and Ephraim, because the house of Joseph is in the north of the land of Israel while Judah is in the Negev. And so it is written: \"Judah stands on its border, from the Negev.\"" "<b>And the stronghold of</b> — construct state, and it does not change, because it is among the forms of reduplication."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 60, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:26.995807919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}